ABSTRACT

The Controlling devices remotely and knowing their real-time state is a common need in homes, hospitals, and industries. We present an ESP32-based relay-control system where commands are sent from a Node-RED dashboard through MQTT topics. The ESP32 subscribes to a command topic (e.g., esp32/relay/cmd), switches the relay accordingly, and publishes its state to a status topic (e.g., esp32/relay/status), so the dashboard always shows live relay status and device online/offline state. An emergency push button triggers an alert that automatically activates the relay, buzzer, and LEDs. The Blynk control, ThingSpeak provides live graphs, and Google Sheets logs every event with a timestamp. The system is built and validated in Wokwi.
